direction: right

title: |md
  ## One tracepoint event, three BPF interfaces
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

kernel: "Kernel TRACE_EVENT" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  body: |md
    `trace_sched_switch(preempt, prev, next)`

    **Does:** marks the scheduler's switch point.
    **Why next:** attached consumers choose how much
    structure they want.
    **State:** original C arguments are still in hand.
  |
}

regular: "SEC(\"tracepoint/sched/sched_switch\")" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  body: |md
    **Does:** kernel copies selected fields into
    `struct trace_event_raw_sched_switch`.

    **State:** stable copied bytes:
    `prev_comm`, `prev_pid`, `next_comm`, ...

    **Tradeoff:** stable format, but no live
    `task_struct *` access.
  |
}

raw: "SEC(\"raw_tracepoint/sched_switch\")" {
  style.fill: "#fde68a"
  body: |md
    **Does:** exposes raw tracepoint args in
    `struct bpf_raw_tracepoint_args`.

    **State:** `ctx->args[0]`, `ctx->args[1]`, ...
    must be decoded by position.

    **Tradeoff:** no copied event struct, but less
    type help than `tp_btf`.
  |
}

btf: "SEC(\"tp_btf/sched_switch\")" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  body: |md
    **Does:** passes BTF-typed tracepoint args:
    `bool preempt`, `task_struct *prev`, `*next`.

    **State:** live typed pointers valid during
    the callback.

    **Tradeoff:** needs kernel BTF and CO-RE care
    for struct fields.
  |
}

kernel -> regular: "copy event fields if regular listeners exist"
kernel -> raw: "pass raw slots"
kernel -> btf: "pass typed args"
